      "displayName": "Chris Wilper",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "[Followup from Sourceforge Tracker]",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Followup Submitter: mrlobo2",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Logged In: YES ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "user_id=1543144",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Originator: NO",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Personally I would much rather see a java based installer (there are several good ones like lzpack and VAinstaller). Web based installers are terribly limited: I have very few good experiences with them. Furthermore, I have told my non-technical collegues that it is pretty easy to look into a simple installation of Fedora. The only thing that I really miss for my collegues is an option in the current installer to ingest the demo object at the end of the quick install and the creation of some icons in their applications folder/start menu.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "A manager web application is nice of course ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "attrs": {
           "id": "1f642",
           "shortName": ":slight_smile:",
           "text": "🙂"
          },
          "type": "emoji"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
